# A web shop handles four personal data breaches. Under Article 33 of the
# GDPR it notifies the supervisory authority within 72 hours of becoming
# aware of a breach, unless the breach is unlikely to result in a risk, and
# a later notice must give reasons; under Article 34 it also tells the
# people affected of a high risk, unless the data was encrypted (Article
# 34(3)(a)). Its hosting processor must inform it of a breach within the
# hours their processing agreement sets.
# The snapshot allows closing only the misdirected email's file without
# notifying the authority, and prohibits it for the other three; it allows
# not telling the owners of the encrypted lost laptop and prohibits it for
# the leaked database; it allows the laptop's notice in time and the
# database's late notice, whose reasons are recorded; and the hosting
# permission does not cover the database leak, whose alert came too late.
# Shows an LE ODRL snapshot with rules: Logical English rules derive the
# requests, their observations and duty evidence from the breach records,
# and the snapshot evaluator decides, with ODRL, DPV and risk prefixes.
# The risk levels are the shop's assessments, given as input.
# Sources https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj (Articles 28, 33, 34)
#         https://www.w3.org/TR/odrl-vocab/
#         https://w3id.org/dpv/2.3/risk/

Use ODRL snapshot logic with namespace "https://example.org/breach-notification#".
Use prefix ex with namespace "https://example.org/breach-notification#".
Use prefix odrl with namespace "http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/".
Use prefix eval with namespace "https://eyereasoner.github.io/eyemind/odrl#".
Use prefix dpv with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv#".
Use prefix pd with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv/pd#".
Use prefix risk with namespace "https://w3id.org/dpv/risk#".

# The breaches, with the shop's risk assessment. Hours count from the
# moment the shop became aware of each breach.

ex:lostLaptop is a risk:DataBreach and ex:lostLaptop has dpv:hasRisk risk:HighRisk.
ex:lostLaptop has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:EmailAddress and ex:lostLaptop has dpv:hasTechnicalMeasure dpv:Encryption.
ex:lostLaptop has ex:authorityNotifiedAt 40.
ex:databaseLeak is a risk:DataBreach and ex:databaseLeak has dpv:hasRisk risk:HighRisk.
ex:databaseLeak has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:MedicalHealth and ex:databaseLeak has ex:authorityNotifiedAt 90.
ex:databaseLeak has ex:processorAlertedAfter 30.
ex:ransomware is a risk:DataBreach and ex:ransomware has dpv:hasRisk risk:ModerateRisk.
ex:ransomware has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:PurchasesAndSpendingHabit and ex:ransomware has ex:processorAlertedAfter 6.
ex:misdirectedEmail is a risk:DataBreach and ex:misdirectedEmail has dpv:hasRisk risk:LowRisk.
ex:misdirectedEmail has dpv:hasPersonalData pd:Name.

# Each breach has a file, the state of the world its requests read, and
# the requests the shop asks about.

ex:lostLaptop has ex:file ex:laptopFile and ex:lostLaptop has ex:closeRequest ex:closeLaptop.
ex:lostLaptop has ex:silenceRequest ex:silenceLaptop and ex:lostLaptop has ex:noticeRequest ex:noticeLaptop.
ex:databaseLeak has ex:file ex:leakFile and ex:databaseLeak has ex:closeRequest ex:closeLeak.
ex:databaseLeak has ex:silenceRequest ex:silenceLeak and ex:databaseLeak has ex:noticeRequest ex:noticeLeak.
ex:databaseLeak has ex:hostingRequest ex:hostingLeak.
ex:ransomware has ex:file ex:ransomwareFile and ex:ransomware has ex:closeRequest ex:closeRansomware.
ex:ransomware has ex:hostingRequest ex:hostingRansomware.
ex:misdirectedEmail has ex:file ex:emailFile and ex:misdirectedEmail has ex:closeRequest ex:closeEmail.
ex:noticeLeak has eval:fulfilledDuty ex:giveReasons.

# The shop's GDPR obligations as an ODRL set, and the processing agreement
# with its hosting processor; a prohibition wins.

ex:evaluation is a eval:Evaluation and ex:evaluation has eval:conflictStrategy odrl:prohibit.
ex:evaluation has eval:policy ex:breachRules and ex:evaluation has eval:policy ex:agreement.

ex:breachRules is a odrl:Set and ex:breachRules has odrl:profile eval:SnapshotProfile.
ex:breachRules has odrl:conflict odrl:prohibit.
ex:breachRules has odrl:permission ex:mayCloseQuietly and ex:breachRules has odrl:prohibition ex:mustNotifyAuthority.
ex:breachRules has odrl:permission ex:mayStaySilent and ex:breachRules has odrl:prohibition ex:mustTellPeople.
ex:breachRules has odrl:permission ex:mayNotifyInTime and ex:breachRules has odrl:permission ex:mayNotifyLate.

# Article 33(1): a file may be closed without notice only when the breach
# is unlikely to result in a risk, which the assessment expresses as low.

ex:mayCloseQuietly is a odrl:Permission and ex:mayCloseQuietly has odrl:assignee ex:webShop.
ex:mayCloseQuietly has odrl:action ex:closeWithoutNotice and ex:mayCloseQuietly has odrl:target ex:breachFile.
ex:mayCloseQuietly has odrl:constraint ex:unlikely.
ex:mustNotifyAuthority is a odrl:Prohibition and ex:mustNotifyAuthority has odrl:assignee ex:webShop.
ex:mustNotifyAuthority has odrl:action ex:closeWithoutNotice and ex:mustNotifyAuthority has odrl:target ex:breachFile.
ex:mustNotifyAuthority has odrl:constraint ex:likely.
ex:unlikely is a odrl:Constraint and ex:unlikely has odrl:leftOperand ex:riskUnlikely.
ex:unlikely has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:unlikely has odrl:rightOperand true.
ex:likely is a odrl:Constraint and ex:likely has odrl:leftOperand ex:riskUnlikely.
ex:likely has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:likely has odrl:rightOperand false.

# Article 34: the people affected need not be told unless they face a high
# risk, which encryption removes.

ex:mayStaySilent is a odrl:Permission and ex:mayStaySilent has odrl:assignee ex:webShop.
ex:mayStaySilent has odrl:action ex:skipTellingPeople and ex:mayStaySilent has odrl:target ex:breachFile.
ex:mayStaySilent has odrl:constraint ex:noHighRisk.
ex:mustTellPeople is a odrl:Prohibition and ex:mustTellPeople has odrl:assignee ex:webShop.
ex:mustTellPeople has odrl:action ex:skipTellingPeople and ex:mustTellPeople has odrl:target ex:breachFile.
ex:mustTellPeople has odrl:constraint ex:highRisk.
ex:noHighRisk is a odrl:Constraint and ex:noHighRisk has odrl:leftOperand ex:peopleAtHighRisk.
ex:noHighRisk has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:noHighRisk has odrl:rightOperand false.
ex:highRisk is a odrl:Constraint and ex:highRisk has odrl:leftOperand ex:peopleAtHighRisk.
ex:highRisk has odrl:operator odrl:eq and ex:highRisk has odrl:rightOperand true.

# Article 33(1): a notice within 72 hours, or a later one with reasons.

ex:mayNotifyInTime is a odrl:Permission and ex:mayNotifyInTime has odrl:assignee ex:webShop.
ex:mayNotifyInTime has odrl:action ex:notifyAuthority and ex:mayNotifyInTime has odrl:target ex:breachFile.
ex:mayNotifyInTime has odrl:constraint ex:inTime.
ex:mayNotifyLate is a odrl:Permission and ex:mayNotifyLate has odrl:assignee ex:webShop.
ex:mayNotifyLate has odrl:action ex:notifyAuthority and ex:mayNotifyLate has odrl:target ex:breachFile.
ex:mayNotifyLate has odrl:constraint ex:late and ex:mayNotifyLate has odrl:duty ex:giveReasons.
ex:inTime is a odrl:Constraint and ex:inTime has odrl:leftOperand ex:hoursToNotice.
ex:inTime has odrl:operator odrl:lteq and ex:inTime has odrl:rightOperand 72.
ex:late is a odrl:Constraint and ex:late has odrl:leftOperand ex:hoursToNotice.
ex:late has odrl:operator odrl:gt and ex:late has odrl:rightOperand 72.
ex:giveReasons is a odrl:Duty and ex:giveReasons has odrl:action ex:explainDelay.

# Article 28: the host may use the customer data under the duty to inform
# the shop of a breach, within the hours the agreement's terms set.

ex:agreement is a odrl:Agreement and ex:agreement has odrl:profile eval:SnapshotProfile.
ex:agreement has odrl:assigner ex:webShop and ex:agreement has odrl:permission ex:hosting.
ex:hosting is a odrl:Permission and ex:hosting has odrl:assignee ex:cloudHost.
ex:hosting has odrl:action odrl:use and ex:hosting has odrl:target ex:customerData.
ex:hosting has odrl:duty ex:alertShop.
ex:alertShop is a odrl:Duty and ex:alertShop has odrl:action odrl:inform.
ex:alertTerms has ex:informWithinHours 24.

# The requests, one family per question.

For every B and Q and F,
if B has ex:closeRequest Q and B has ex:file F
then ex:evaluation has eval:request Q and Q is a eval:Request and Q has odrl:assignee ex:webShop and
Q has odrl:action ex:closeWithoutNotice and Q has odrl:target ex:breachFile and Q has eval:state F.
For every B and Q and F,
if B has ex:silenceRequest Q and B has ex:file F
then ex:evaluation has eval:request Q and Q is a eval:Request and Q has odrl:assignee ex:webShop and
Q has odrl:action ex:skipTellingPeople and Q has odrl:target ex:breachFile and Q has eval:state F.
For every B and Q and F,
if B has ex:noticeRequest Q and B has ex:file F
then ex:evaluation has eval:request Q and Q is a eval:Request and Q has odrl:assignee ex:webShop and
Q has odrl:action ex:notifyAuthority and Q has odrl:target ex:breachFile and Q has eval:state F.
For every B and Q and F,
if B has ex:hostingRequest Q and B has ex:file F
then ex:evaluation has eval:request Q and Q is a eval:Request and Q has odrl:assignee ex:cloudHost and
Q has odrl:action odrl:use and Q has odrl:target ex:customerData and Q has eval:state F.
For every Q, if Q is a eval:Request then Q has eval:subject ex:customers.

# Each file's observations, derived from its breach record as true or false.

For every B and F,
if B has ex:file F
then F is a eval:State and F has eval:subject ex:customers.
For every B and F,
if B has ex:file F and B has dpv:hasRisk risk:LowRisk
then F has ex:riskUnlikely true.
For every B and F,
if B has ex:file F and it is not known that B has dpv:hasRisk risk:LowRisk
then F has ex:riskUnlikely false.
For every B and F,
if B has ex:file F and B has dpv:hasRisk risk:HighRisk and
it is not known that B has dpv:hasTechnicalMeasure dpv:Encryption
then F has ex:peopleAtHighRisk true.
For every B and F,
if B has ex:file F and it is not known that F has ex:peopleAtHighRisk true
then F has ex:peopleAtHighRisk false.
For every B and F and H,
if B has ex:file F and B has ex:authorityNotifiedAt H
then F has ex:hoursToNotice H.

# The processor's duty evidence, from the hours the agreement allows.

For every B and Q and H and L,
if B has ex:hostingRequest Q and B has ex:processorAlertedAfter H and
ex:alertTerms has ex:informWithinHours L and H is at most L
then Q has eval:fulfilledDuty ex:alertShop.
For every B and Q and H and L,
if B has ex:hostingRequest Q and B has ex:processorAlertedAfter H and
ex:alertTerms has ex:informWithinHours L and H is greater than L
then Q has eval:unfulfilledDuty ex:alertShop.
